<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:zap="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Zapit;assembly=OpenRigs.Zapit"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:zdq="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Opto.ZapitBonsai;assembly=OpenRigs.Opto.ZapitBonsai"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>Zapit's setup phase, between launch and Go, inside ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's Zapit group: the protocol is lib-open-rigs' docs/zapit-setup-protocol.md. Declares the device Zapit-Main's commands (DeclareDeviceControls): Zapit-Main.Setup (args: a grid run folder in RigConfigs\&lt;RIG&gt;\pending holding the agent's grid.json) points the galvos at each point, saving point_NNNN.png and background_K.png there (ZapitSetupCapture); Zapit-Main.Still (args: a new .png in pending) saves the next camera frame, laser off; Zapit-Main.LoadBank (args: the bank's Settings_ZapitBank_&lt;DateTime&gt;.json in pending) loads it into ZapitDaq (ZapitSetupCapture checks the path), which publishes it on Zapit.Bank; Zapit-Main.LaserOff zeroes every line at once, before or after Go, and refuses a grid run or still in progress ("Refused Laser Off came during a setup step: the lines are zeroed and nothing more is saved for &lt;folder or png&gt;", camera settings put back, the run ending there, not pointing the beam again, no aim held). Zapit-Main.Aim (args: xVolts,yVolts,laserVolts) points the beam by hand, reported on its own metric Zapit-Main.Aim ("Aiming &lt;volts&gt;", "Off Go", "Off Laser Off" (Laser Off always sends a Zero of its own, so with no step running the metric shows it), "Off no aim for 10 s" (an aim not renewed within 10 s is zeroed: the aim watchdog) or "Refused &lt;why&gt;", ZapitDaq's own refusal of the Point while a play is armed included: "Refused ZapitDaq cannot Point while Play Condition is armed") so the Setup metric keeps BankLoaded; refused at rig.yml zapit.ceilingMw 0, above laserMinMaxControlVolts[1] (both from ZapitRig), above the ceiling's volts (Zapit.LaserCeilingVolts, ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's launch property LaserCeilingVolts) or during a grid run or still; a grid's laserVolts is held to the same rules; at Go a beam still aimed is zeroed, and a grid run or still in progress refused with the lines zeroed. A grid.json whose skipFrames is not a whole number from 0 to 100 or whose backgrounds is not a whole number from 1 to 100 is refused naming grid.json and the field. A grid run with no Pointed within 2 s of its start or no camera frame within 2 s of Pointed (or of its last frame), and a still with no camera frame in 2 s, is refused. Setup, Still and LoadBank are taken until Go (ExperimentGo) and ignored after it. Each stage is reported as the metric Zapit-Main.Setup: "Pointing &lt;folder&gt;", "FramesSaved &lt;folder&gt;", "StillSaved &lt;png&gt;", "Loading &lt;json&gt;", "BankLoaded &lt;json&gt;" or "Refused &lt;why&gt;", each stage before its command goes to ZapitDaq, whose answer (BankLoaded comes back inside LoadBank) must not be overwritten by it; a refused request leaves the workflow running. A grid.json camera block's exposure and gain go to the Zapit camera with the run's first point, and its session settings back with the run's end, on Camera-Zapit.Settings (ZapitCamera's ZapitPylonCapture). Zapit-Main.Play (args: condition,powerMw,seconds) is Play Condition (ZapitPlay; open_rigs.zapit.play drives the sequence): ZapitDaq's own Arm of that condition from the loaded bank as trial 0, refused (never an error) with no bank, a play already armed, the laser disabled, or a condition, power or duration the bank and maxTrialSeconds cannot play (a play whose rows exceed the cap, however long, as "Refused a Zapit trial of &lt;seconds&gt; s with its ramp is longer than maxTrialSeconds (&lt;n&gt; s)"; a missing condition as "Refused the Zapit waveforms have no condition 4; they have 3"), reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Play (Arming, Armed, Playing, Ended, Off or Refused); Zapit-Main.Trigger (args: on, else off) raises or clears the ZapitTrigger line on BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands (SetZapitTriggerLine; the twin's trigger with on), which starts the armed play on the NI DAQ's trigger terminal as a trial's trigger does; the line is cleared by LaserOff before Go, by the play's end (its own, a stop or a Zero) and at every Go (a play still armed has its lines zeroed too), and by the board itself its pulse width after it rose (ZapitTriggerLine). Play and Trigger are taken until Go and ignored after it. Zapit-Main.Crop (args: #n x,y,w,h in pixels of the camera's frame, or #n full; n a whole number from 1, echoed in every answer) cuts the Zapit camera's viewed frame, for viewing only, before or after Go (the mp4 stays whole; ZapitCropRequest, on Camera-Zapit.Settings to ZapitCamera), reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Crop ("Cropping #n &lt;x,y,w,h&gt;" or "Cropping #n Full Frame" when taken, then the camera's answer from its next frame: "Cropped #n &lt;x,y,w,h&gt;", "Full Frame #n", "Refused #n &lt;why&gt;; Now Full Frame" or "Refused #n &lt;why&gt;; Now Cropped &lt;x,y,w,h&gt;"; no valid number is #0). It cuts the live view (View), and the recording too (Image) when rig.yml's zapit.camera.recordCrop is true, the default: then from Go each request is refused ("Refused #n the crop is recorded ... ; Now ...", CropRecorded? sets CropRequest's Fixed), so the recording, which starts at Go, keeps one frame size; with recordCrop false it cuts the live view only and is taken before and after Go. Stills and grid runs save Camera-Zapit.Data's Still, the whole frame (a grid run's at Mono8's scale), never the cropped View. A bank ZapitDaq refuses (hash, sample rate, a volt outside +/-10 V) stops the workflow naming it. Needs ControlEvents, ExperimentGo, RigFile, ZapitRig, Zapit.LaserCeilingVolts, Zapit.Commands, Zapit.Events, Zapit.Bank, Camera-Zapit.Settings, Camera-Zapit.Data, ZapitTriggerLine and BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands from the workflow.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Setup</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Still</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Camera-Zapit.Data</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Value.Still</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>RigFile</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
        <scr:Name>PendingFolder</scr:Name>
        <scr:Expression>it.Substring(0, it.LastIndexOf(Convert.ToChar(92)) + 1) + "pending"</scr:Expression>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="PendingFolder" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitSetupCapture">
          <zap:PendingFolder>UNMAPPED</zap:PendingFolder>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCommand?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Command != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Command</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Setup</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>LoadBank</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>LaserOff</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:CreateZapitDaqCommand" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>BankLoaded?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Kind == "BankLoaded"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Bank</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Bank</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
        <scr:Expression>"BankLoaded " + JsonPath</scr:Expression>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Setup</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:DeclareDeviceControls">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Parameters />
          <orcl:Commands>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Setup</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Run the scanner grid in the pending folder named (its grid.json): a frame per point, then laser-off backgrounds. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Still</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Save the next Zapit camera frame, laser off, as the pending .png named. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>LoadBank</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Load the session's bank (Settings_ZapitBank_&lt;DateTime&gt;.json) into ZapitDaq. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>LaserOff</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Stop any Zapit output at once: galvos, laser and LED at 0 V, ending a grid run or still in progress.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Aim</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Point the beam by hand: args xVolts,yVolts,laserVolts (the agent's, through the scanner fit and laser curve). Refused at ceilingMw 0, above laserMinMaxControlVolts[1] or during a grid run or still; LaserOff ends it. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Play</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Play Condition: args condition,powerMw,seconds. Arms that condition's trial from the loaded bank as ZapitDaq arms a task's (trial 0), at one of its powers (at most ceilingMw), lasting seconds with its ramp; Trigger on starts it. Reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Play (Arming, Armed, Playing, Ended, Off or Refused). Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Trigger</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Raise or clear the ZapitTrigger line (and the masking light): args on raises it, starting an armed play; anything else clears it. Cleared too by LaserOff and when the play ends. Before Go only.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
            <orcl:Command>
              <orcl:Name>Crop</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Description>Cut the Zapit camera's live view (and its mp4 when rig.yml's zapit.camera.recordCrop is true, the default), to args #n x,y,w,h (pixels of the camera's frame; x and y from 0, w and h even and from 16), or to the whole frame for #n full, n a whole number from 1; the stills stay whole. Reported on the metric Zapit-Main.Crop with n echoed: Cropping #n when taken, then the camera's answer from the next frame (Cropped #n x,y,w,h, Full Frame #n, or Refused #n &lt;why&gt;; Now Full Frame or Now Cropped x,y,w,h for the crop in force); no valid number is Refused #0. A recorded crop is refused from Go (Refused #n the crop is recorded ...; Now ...); a view-only crop (recordCrop false) is taken before and after Go.</orcl:Description>
            </orcl:Command>
          </orcl:Commands>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCamera?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Camera != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Camera</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Camera-Zapit.Settings</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Aim</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ZapitRig</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="CeilingMw" Selector="LaserCeilingMw" />
          <Property Name="LaserMaxVolts" Selector="LaserMaxControlVolts" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>Aim?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Aim</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Aim</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCommand?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Command != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Command</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>SetupStep?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>!Aim</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.LaserCeilingVolts</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="LaserCeilingVolts" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Play</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ZapitRig</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="MaxTrialSeconds" Selector="MaxTrialSeconds" />
          <Property Name="CeilingMw" Selector="LaserCeilingMw" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>PlayCondition</Name>
        <Description>Play Condition before Go (open_rigs.zapit.play drives it): each Zapit-Main.Play request (condition,powerMw,seconds) becomes ZapitDaq's own Arm of that condition from the loaded bank (trial 0), or is refused; its stages reported as Zapit-Main.Play before the Arm goes to ZapitDaq.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitPlay">
          <zap:MaxTrialSeconds>0</zap:MaxTrialSeconds>
          <zap:CeilingMw>0</zap:CeilingMw>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Play</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCommand?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Command != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Command</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>PlayOver?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Stage == "Ended" || Stage == "Off"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>The play over (Ended, or Off at Go): the ZapitTrigger line cleared here, a backstop to the agent's own clear.</Description>
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Trigger</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>On?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>it.Trim() == "on"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>Play Condition's start: the ZapitTrigger line raised, as a trial's trigger raises it (the masking light with it).</Description>
        <Set>true</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>TwinTrigger</Name>
        <Description>The simulated twin's trigger edge with the line, as ZapitDaqTrials sends it; the NI DAQ ignores it.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="zdq:ZapitTwinTrigger" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Zapit.Commands</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>Off?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>it.Trim() != "on"</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>Zapit-Main.Trigger off (anything but on): the ZapitTrigger line cleared.</Description>
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>Zapit-Main.LaserOff before Go: the ZapitTrigger line cleared with the outputs zeroed.</Description>
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceCommand">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Command>Crop</orcl:Command>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>CropRequest</Name>
        <Description>Zapit-Main.Crop: the viewed frame's crop (x,y,w,h, or the whole frame), and the recorded frame's when rig.yml's zapit.camera.recordCrop is true (the default; from Go then refused, CropRecorded? setting Fixed), reported as Zapit-Main.Crop (Cropping, then the camera's answer) and sent to the camera on Camera-Zapit.Settings.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitCropRequest" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Crop</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>HasCamera?</Name>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Camera != null</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Camera</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>Camera-Zapit.Settings</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Camera-Zapit.Data</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Value.CropReports</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Name>CropReport</Name>
        <Description>The camera's answer to a crop, from the first frame cut to it: Cropped #n, Full Frame #n, or Refused #n (a crop outside the frame, then shown whole; or a request that was no crop, the crop kept) with "; Now Full Frame" or "; Now Cropped x,y,w,h" for the crop in force; the metric reads Cropping until then.</Description>
        <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitCropReport" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
          <orcl:Name>Zapit-Main.Crop</orcl:Name>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SetZapitTriggerLine.bonsai">
        <Description>Go: the ZapitTrigger line cleared, whatever the setup left it at (Trigger on with no play armed, or after its end), so the first trial's trigger is an edge.</Description>
        <Set>false</Set>
        <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ZapitRig</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
        <Name>CropRecorded?</Name>
        <Description>Go on a rig whose Zapit camera records its crop (rig.yml's zapit.camera.recordCrop, the default): CropRequest's Fixed is set, so each later crop is refused by the camera naming the crop in force, and the mp4 keeps one frame size. The crop chain is never ended, so Camera-Zapit.Settings stays open for the setup's Restore.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
              <Name>Source1</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Item2.Camera != null &amp;&amp; Item2.Camera.RecordCrop</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="Fixed" Selector="Item2.Camera.RecordCrop" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="7" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
